// handler for the model's refund call; the service token behind it can read
// and write every order in the tenant
export async function issueRefund({ orderId, cents }: Args) {
  return refunds.create({ orderId, cents });
}
```

A customer asks the agent to refund an order that belongs to a different customer. The model has no other context and proposes the call. Where must the refusal happen?

```ts
async function refundWithRetry(orderId: string, cents: number) {
  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= 3; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await payments.refund({ orderId, cents, idempotencyKey: `${runId}:${attempt}` });
    } catch (err) {
      if (attempt === 3) throw err;
    }
  }
}
```

The first attempt times out after the provider has already charged, so attempt 2 charges again. The provider supports idempotency keys. What fixes it?

